---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CiYamlValidator from '../../components/CiYamlValidator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="CI/CD YAML Validator" description="Check a GitHub Actions workflow YAML for common structural issues before pushing.">
  <CiYamlValidator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why catch YAML issues before pushing</h2>
  <p>A broken GitHub Actions workflow often fails silently or produces confusing errors only visible in the Actions tab after a push — catching structural issues (bad indentation, missing required keys) locally saves a round trip of push-check-fix cycles.</p>

  <h2>How to use this validator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste your workflow YAML.</li>
    <li>Review flagged structural issues (indentation, missing keys, invalid syntax).</li>
    <li>Fix and re-check before committing.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Inconsistent indentation</strong> — YAML is whitespace-sensitive, and mixing tabs and spaces (or inconsistent space counts) is a frequent source of parse errors.</li>
    <li><strong>Missing required top-level keys</strong> like <code>on:</code> or <code>jobs:</code>, causing the workflow to not trigger at all.</li>
    <li><strong>Incorrect indentation under <code>steps:</code></strong>, which can silently nest steps under the wrong job.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sanity-checking a workflow file before committing</li>
    <li>Debugging why a GitHub Actions workflow isn't triggering</li>
    <li>Reviewing a workflow file in a pull request</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does this validate against GitHub's full schema?</strong> It checks common structural issues, not the complete GitHub Actions schema — for full validation, GitHub's own workflow editor provides real-time schema checking.</p>
</ToolLayout>
